LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","review_id":"CBxExSI9RRwPpc7jqdgDsQ","date":"2010-02-04T13:44:31","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9495221376419067,"text_excerpt":"A New Orleans staple. This place has been around for years. The concierge recommended Bon Ton cafe. Also, our coworker called his NO native father in law who told him we made the right choice. We loved it so much that when our partners asked us for dinner the next evening - location Bon Ton again.. we sure didn't mind. Must Haves: Crabmeat Au Gratin - creamy and delicious.. The serving isn't huge; justs an FYI.. This dish was on food network as one of the best. You can't argue with the Food Network. Asparagus on mixed greens - best dressing ever! DELICIOUS Turtle Soup - yep, it's made with turtles.. sounds yucks but it was my fav. I ordered it on my second visit as well. Day #1: we ordere..."},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","review_id":"eEjkyu_0vm948CxbY7bv0Q","date":"2013-01-10T14:59:36","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9434404373168945,"text_excerpt":"This place is old school New Orleans dining, featuring a Cajun/Creole menu replete with all of the old classics that make eating out in this town such a singular experience. We started with fried crawfish tails, which were perfectly fried and yummy. The two fish dishes I tried here...Drum topped with grilled Gulf oysters and Redfish Bon Ton...were up there with the best and freshest I've had in Louisiana. The grilled oysters on the filet of drum were amazing; perfectly cooked and deliciously flavored with butter and lemon. They have a menu item that features these little beauties as the main protein, and I may have to get that on my next visit. The fish Bon Ton features a Creole sauce wit..."},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","review_id":"v-kLWfAqm_nsXdSUSXqB1Q","date":"2011-11-07T19:53:13","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9433680772781372,"text_excerpt":"Mmmm, here we go. I love good food, and a restaurant that not only knows the quality of good food, but the clientele that they are serving, the culture of their city, and the value of outstanding service is #1 in my book. We were given a heads up on this place, from a Denver local who happened to be sitting next to us at Camilla, another favorite eatery in Nola. So, it was at the top of the must try list. Turns out it was right around the corner from the hotel and had a great ambiance. I started out with a glass of wine, but was enticed into the signature drink by everyone in the joint that had one in hand. It wasn't my favorite, but I love a place that has a specialty. Classic. I also he..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","photo_id":"UMlMewkgFANcLLfadE1Qdw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/UMlMewkgFANcLLfadE1Qdw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8967597484588623},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","photo_id":"zZuz82f_AIayelnTxmBpGA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/zZuz82f_AIayelnTxmBpGA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.889790415763855},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","photo_id":"OQ8zUfiNit4OEFna6JYxpQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/OQ8zUfiNit4OEFna6JYxpQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8645334243774414},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SISqtAAA","photo_id":"jZt3FoyuHQnX2mmTu4XfLA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/jZt3FoyuHQnX2mmTu4XfLA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8550649285316467},{"business_id":"qjP2XXjtLdlZ20SIS